    "lawCode": "Amd §§499-a, 499-b, 499-c, 499-f, 499-i & 499-j, Judy L",
    "lawSection": "Judiciary Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S3934\n\nSPONSOR: BAILEY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the judiciary law, in relation to the state commission\non prosecutorial conduct\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThe purpose of this legislation is to update provisions of law relating\nto the commission on prosecutorial conduct, to serve as a factfinding\nentity designated to review complaints of prosecutorial misconduct in\nNew York State and produce a factual record and recommendations, in\norder to improve Appellate Division attorney grievance committees'\ndisciplinary oversight of district attorneys and assistant district\nattorneys and to improve the exercise of the Governor's authority to\nremove district attorneys.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one of the bill amends Article 15-A of the Judiciary Law, §\n499-a, to clarify the responsibilities of the Commission on Prosecutori-\nal Conduct.\n\nSection two of the bill, amending § 499-b, clarifies relevant defi-\nnitions for the purposes of the article.\n\nSection three of the bill amends § 499-c to correct a cross-citation.\n\nSection four of the bill amends § 499-f, updating provisions related to\nthe transmittal of the commission's factual record, its recommendations,\nand the record of its proceedings and deleting vestigial provisions.\n\nSection five of the bill amends § 499-i in relation to the responsibil-\nities of the appellate division and the commission in these matters.\n\nSection six of the bill deletes a vestigial provision from § 499-j.\n\nSection seven of the bill declares the legislative intent that any\nprovision of Article 15-A may be severed without permanent injunction of\nthe remainder.\n\nSection eight of the bill, a severance clause, provides that if any part\nof the act shall be adjudged as unconstitutional or invalid, it shall\nnot affect or impair any other part or provision of this act, but shall\nbe confined in its operation to such part or provision.\n\nSection nine of the bill provides the effective date. JUSTIFICATION:\nThese amendments clarify and update provisions of law related to the\nState Commission on Prosecutorial Conduct's authority to investigate,\nmake factual findings and refer those findings and its recommendations\nto the attorney grievance committees of the Appellate Division and to\nthe Governor. The amendments update related provisions throughout the\narticle.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n\n2019-20: S.8815/A.10805a(Perry)- Referred to Rules FISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately\n",
